<include>
  <!--
    Twilio Elastic SIP Trunking — outbound termination.

    Twilio terminates against a Termination SIP URI provisioned in the console
    (Elastic SIP Trunking → Trunks → Termination), which looks like
    `<your-trunk>.pstn.twilio.com`. That hostname is both the proxy and the
    digest realm, so TWILIO_SIP_TERMINATION_DOMAIN is the one variable that has
    to be right; leaving it unset resolves this gateway to a hostname that does
    not exist and every leg fails with NO_ROUTE_DESTINATION.

    Auth is by Credential List, by IP ACL, or by both:

      Credential List  set TWILIO_SIP_USERNAME / TWILIO_SIP_PASSWORD to the
                       credential you created under Elastic SIP Trunking →
                       Authentication. Twilio challenges with 407 and this
                       gateway answers.
      IP ACL           leave the credentials unset and add this host's public
                       SIP IP to the trunk's Access Control List. No gateway
                       setting substitutes for that entry.

    register MUST stay false. Twilio trunks are terminated against, never
    registered to, and a REGISTER attempt is refused.

    Number format: Twilio requires E.164 with the leading `+`, which is why the
    TWILIO carrier's gateway row is seeded `E164`. A bare 1XXXXXXXXXX is
    rejected with 404.

    Caller ID: Twilio only allows a From number the account owns (a Twilio DID
    or a Verified Caller ID). Presenting someone else's number is refused
    outright, so the TWILIO carrier is seeded POOL against `twilio` DIDs —
    calls that fall to this carrier swap to a number it issued.
  -->
  <gateway name="twilio">
    <param name="proxy" value="$${twilio_sip_proxy}"/>
    <param name="realm" value="$${twilio_sip_realm}"/>
    <param name="from-domain" value="$${twilio_sip_realm}"/>
    <param name="username" value="$${twilio_sip_user}"/>
    <param name="password" value="$${twilio_sip_pass}"/>
    <param name="register" value="false"/>
    <param name="caller-id-in-from" value="true"/>
    <param name="ping" value="25"/>
  </gateway>
</include>
